--   2. *Birth history.* In the ideal experiment (seed, Haar frames $U,V$ and Gaussian tensors of every label, mutually independent) the simulator's state before stage $k$ is born is $\mathcal G_{<k}$-measurable, where $\mathcal G_{<k}$ (133) is generated by the seed, $U$, $v_{<k}$ and all earlier-stage tensors.
--   3. *Birth law.* $v_k$ is conditionally uniform on the residual unit sphere orthogonal to $v_{<k}$: $\mathbb E[f(v_k)\mid\mathcal G_{<k}]=\int f\,d\pi_{v_{<k}}$ for bounded measurable $f$.
