--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: the simulator has the failure and crossing responses (131), (132) → the identities static mean = (131)/(132) and static noise = prefix noise (42) under |w_i| < 1/4 for i > k; reason: the simulator's responses are (131)/(132) by definition; their agreement with the static oracle is the lemma's content (pp.67–68)
--   - generalization: orthonormal frames → the identities of part 1 for arbitrary frames; reason: purely algebraic; specializes to orthonormal frames
