-- source:
--   Xia, Yuan, On Global Joint Lower Bounds in Zeroth-Order Nonconvex Optimization, arXiv:2610.19652, Lemma E.2, p.67, (130)–(136)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ZOGlobalLB_IsHaarFrame
import Definitions.Def_ZOGlobalLB_Simulator

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal

namespace ZOGlobalLB

/-- **Lemma E.2 (Prefix simulator and conditional birth law).** Xia, Yuan, arXiv:2610.19652,
Lemma E.2, p.67, (130)–(136).

The disclosed-prefix simulator has the failure and crossing responses (131) and (132). At stage
`k`'s birth, `v_k` is conditionally Haar in dimension `m - k + 1`, and its label-stage arrays are
fresh and independent of the birth history. These assertions hold under the unconditioned field
law.

Stated in four parts (0-based stage `k : Fin T`, the paper's stage `k + 1`):
1. *Responses.* If the undisclosed chain coordinates are small, `|w_i| < 1/4` for all `i > k`,
   the static mean `F_new(z, x)` equals the failure mean (131) when the stage-`k` gate fails and
   the crossing mean (132) when it holds, and the static noise `N_j(w, x)` of (34) equals the
   prefix noise (42) (pp.67–68: "equality with the static mean is algebraically exact under the
   stated projection condition").
2. *Birth history* (134). In the ideal experiment (seed `X₀`, Haar frames `U`, `V`, independent
   Gaussian tensors `G` of every label, mutually independent), the simulator state after each
   test count `t` at which stage `k` is not yet born before `t` is `G_{<k}`-measurable, so the
   history up to the birth of stage `k` is.
3. *Birth law* (135). For bounded measurable `f`, `E[f(v_k) | G_{<k}] = ∫ f dπ_{v_{<k}}`, the
   uniform law on the residual sphere orthogonal to `v_{<k}` (dimension `m - k` in 0-based terms,
   `m - k + 1` in the paper's).
4. *Fresh arrays.* The stage-`k` tensors of all labels have their original standard Gaussian law
   and are independent of `G_{<k} ∨ σ(v_k)`.

**Formalization Note.** Part 1 holds for arbitrary frames (`generalization`; the paper's frames are
orthonormal). Parts 3–4 condition on the enlarged `G_{<k}` (133), which contains the birth
history by part 2; the conditional law given the birth history follows by the tower property, as
in the paper. Conditional expectations are taken with respect to `G_{<k}`, which is a
sub-σ-algebra because all random elements are measurable. -/
theorem lemma_E_2 {r m T : ℕ} {σ : ℝ} (hσ : 0 < σ) :
    (∀ (U : Fin T → E r) (V : Fin T → E m) (k : Fin T) (z : E r) (x : E m),
      (∀ i : Fin T, k < i → |wcoord U z i| < 1 / 4) →
      (¬ gateS U V k z x → FnewZX U V z x = failMean U V k z x) ∧
      (gateS U V k z x → FnewZX U V z x = crossMean U V k z x) ∧
      ∀ G : Fin T × Idx m → ℝ,
        noiseN σ V G (wcoord U z) x = prefixNoise σ V k G (wcoord U z) x) ∧
    ∀ {J S₀ : Type*} [MeasurableSpace J] [Countable J] [MeasurableSingletonClass J]
      [MeasurableSpace S₀] {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
      [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
      (X₀ : Ω → S₀) (U : Ω → Fin T → E r) (V : Ω → Fin T → E m)
      (G : Ω → J × (Fin T × Idx m) → ℝ),
      Measurable X₀ → IsHaarFrame P U → IsHaarFrame P V → Measurable G →
      HasLaw G (gaussArr (J × (Fin T × Idx m))) P →
      (IndepFun X₀ (fun ω => (U ω, V ω, G ω)) P ∧ IndepFun U (fun ω => (V ω, G ω)) P ∧
        IndepFun V G P) →
      ∀ (B : SimAlg r m J S₀) (k : Fin T),
        (∀ t : ℕ, Measurable[Gless X₀ U V G k] (fun ω =>
          if ∀ t' < t, (simState B σ (U ω) (V ω) (G ω) (X₀ ω) t').1 < k then
            simState B σ (U ω) (V ω) (G ω) (X₀ ω) t
          else (0, false, 0))) ∧
        (∀ f : E m → ℝ, Measurable f → (∃ C, ∀ y, |f y| ≤ C) →
          P[fun ω => f (V ω k) | Gless X₀ U V G k] =ᵐ[P]
            fun ω => ∫ y, f y ∂(residualUnif (V ω) k)) ∧
        HasLaw (fun ω (p : J × Idx m) => G ω (p.1, (k, p.2))) (gaussArr (J × Idx m)) P ∧
        Indep (MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (p : J × Idx m) => G ω (p.1, (k, p.2))) inferInstance)
          (Gless X₀ U V G k ⊔ MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => V ω k) inferInstance) P := by sorry

end ZOGlobalLB
